// Probes for category: math
// 11 atoms × 15 probes (5 per L1/L2/L3) = 165 probes
// Scorer types used: exact_match_string, exact_match_numeric, regex, mcq_letter, set_equal, substring_any, substring_all, judge_rubric
//
// === Subagent review (v1) — fixes applied (v2) ===
// FIXED:
//   - math.symbolic_manipulation.L1.004: regex now requires distinct 3 and 4 (no longer accepts (x-3)(x-3))
//   - math.series_limit_eval.L3.004: regex now accepts both ln(2) and log(2) (prompt invited both)
//   - math.proof_construction.L3.001: substring 'finite' replaced with 'only finitely many' (prior leaked through 'infinitely'); dropped fragile '+ 1' literal
//   - math.proof_construction.L1.004: replaced trivial divisibility-counting probe with a genuine proof-completion step (sum of evens)
//   - math.modular_arithmetic.L3.001: replaced divisor-list probe (no modular reasoning) with a polynomial-remainder count (n²≡4 mod 7)
//   - math.polynomial_root_theory.L1.002: changed polynomial to 2x²+5x-3 (was duplicate of L1.001)
//   - math.optimization_extremum.L3.004: replaced trivial perimeter/area probe with weighted AM-GM (xyz=8 ⇒ min x+2y+4z=12)
//
// DECLINED (documented):
//   - math.proof_construction L1/L2 (other probes): retained as fill-in / definitional probes. Truly free-form proof construction
//     cannot be deterministically scored at L1/L2 difficulty without judge_rubric, which the spec asks me to use sparingly.
//     L3 covers the genuine proof-writing surface with substring_all + 1 judge_rubric.
//   - math.complex_number_geometry L1.002 / L1.004 / L2.003 / L2.004 / L3.003: kept. These test the encoding/computation
//     side of the atom (modulus, multiplication, distance under complex notation), which is the L1 verb of the atom.
//   - math.synthetic_geometry uses 13-14-15 triangle in two probes: kept; this triple is canonical-textbook, not unique to AIME.
//   - Some symbolic-regex scorers reject Unicode superscripts (²/³). Accepted; prompts state ASCII-form output (e.g. 'in standard form').
//   - Within-level monotony (e.g. all 5 series_limit_eval L2 use partial fractions): partly inherent to the atom's L2 axis,
//     which IS partial-fractions / telescoping. Surface domains vary.
//
// Notes:
//   - judge_rubric used 1× total (math.proof_construction.L3.005 — vacuous truth)
//   - substring_all used 4× (Euclid, sqrt(2), induction, divisibility) — documented gameability tradeoff
//   - For numeric answers prefer exact_match_numeric (tolerance=0 unless irrational decimal required)
//   - For symbolic answers prefer regex with explicit form instructions in the prompt
{"probe_id":"math.symbolic_manipulation.L1.001","canonical_id":"math.symbolic_manipulation","category":"math","level":"L1","axis_values":{"expression_size":"small","operation":"expand"},"prompt":"Expand the product (x+3)(x-3). Output only the expanded polynomial in standard form.","ground_truth":"x^2 - 9","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"^\\s*x\\s*(?:\\^\\s*2|²)\\s*[-−]\\s*9\\s*$","flags":["i"],"allow_symbolic_equivalence":false},"tags":["math","symbolic","expand"],"notes":"L1 difference of squares; representation is part of the contract"}
{"probe_id":"math.symbolic_manipulation.L1.002","canonical_id":"math.symbolic_manipulation","category":"math","level":"L1","axis_values":{"expression_size":"small","operation":"simplify"},"prompt":"Simplify a^5 / a^2 (assume a ≠ 0). Output only the simplified expression.","ground_truth":"a^3","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"^\\s*a\\s*\\^?\\s*3\\s*$","flags":["i"]},"tags":["math","symbolic","simplify"],"notes":""}
