{"probe_id":"math.equation_solve.L3.005","canonical_id":"math.equation_solve","category":"math","level":"L3","axis_values":{"equation_class":"transcendental_single"},"prompt":"Solve the equation e^(2x) − 5 e^x + 6 = 0 for real x. Output the smaller of the two solutions in exact form (e.g. 'ln(2)').","ground_truth":"ln(2)","scorer":{"type":"regex","pattern":"^\\s*(?:ln\\s*\\(?\\s*2\\s*\\)?|log\\s*_?\\s*e\\s*\\(?\\s*2\\s*\\)?)\\s*$","flags":["i"]},"tags":["math","equation","transcendental","substitution"],"notes":"Let u=e^x: u²-5u+6=0 ⇒ u=2,3 ⇒ x=ln(2) or ln(3). Smaller is ln(2)"}
